    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Gravity-driven deformation in a variety of geologic settings typically leads to “Scoop-shaped” failures, suggesting a common mechanical process may operate. This paper proposes a study of the development of failure surfaces associated with landslides and listric normal faults. Although there has been extensive research on both of these phenomena, few studies have investigated the mechanics behind the development of their scoop-shaped geometry or integrated studies of a variety of phenomena to try to reach a general understanding of why scoop-shaped failures form. The proposed project will integrate structural mapping, deformation mapping of active structures, and numerical modeling to better understand the process of gravity-driven failure.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
